From: Madhurkiran Harikrishnan <madhurkiran.harikrishnan@xilinx.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Sep 2018 14:08:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] qwaylandeglwindow: Bind context before eglDestroySurface

Call eglMakeCurrent to bind the context to the current rendering thread
before calling eglDestroySurface to avoid a crash caused by post-processing
activity in the GPU driver.

In Qt6, qwaylandeglwindow.cpp moved from the qtwayland module into
qtbase (src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/).
The fix is otherwise identical to the Qt5 version.

Signed-off-by: Madhurkiran Harikrishnan <madhurkiran.harikrishnan@xilinx.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp        | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/qwaylandeglwindow.cpp
@@ -143,6 +143,8 @@ void QWaylandEglWindow::invalidateSurface()
     QMutexLocker lock (&m_eglSurfaceLock);

     if (m_eglSurface) {
+        eglMakeCurrent(m_clientBufferIntegration->eglDisplay(), EGL_NO_SURFACE,
+                       EGL_NO_SURFACE, EGL_NO_CONTEXT);
         eglDestroySurface(m_clientBufferIntegration->eglDisplay(), m_eglSurface);
         m_eglSurface = 0;
     }
